                                "sense_id": "0d5ed18c-96a3-3202-beee-afe4fba3d469",
                                "text": "[…] if a Parliament be triable and arraignable before the King himselfe: Then hath the King an unlimited declarative power of Law above all Courts, in his own breast;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed819ed8-0efc-4a0b-8b02-108c7fcf7169",
                                "sense_id": "0d5ed18c-96a3-3202-beee-afe4fba3d469",
                                "text": "[…] however I may be arraignable for any Error in my Judgment, I am perfectly free from aught of Sinister in my Intention with regard to the present Matter."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
